# Line endings
#
# Without this file, an editor or tool on Windows can silently rewrite a
# file from LF to CRLF, and git reports every single line as changed.
# That happened once already: 71 files across client/ and server/ showed
# as modified when nothing in them had actually changed.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` means: git decides what's text, stores it with LF,
# and checks it out with LF. One convention everywhere, including on
# Windows. This matches Vite, ESLint and Prettier defaults.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats — git must never try to normalise these.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.pdf   binary
